{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Friends Will Be Friends", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "extraordinary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely good or impressive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Axe throwing is extraordinary.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about plans.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chores", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a routine or minor duties or tasks", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I figure I'll have done all my chores by 10:00 a.m. on Sunday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "axe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a hand tool with one side of its head forged and sharpened to a cutting edge", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are going to go axe throwing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "toss up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a situation in which there is no clear right choice or in which what will happen is not known", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Right now, it's a toss up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on the house", "type": "name"}, {"content": "given away free by a merchant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Didn't I mention that the tickets are on the house?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "baffling", "type": "name"}, {"content": "making great mental demands; hard to comprehend or solve or believe", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are truly baffling.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision or an observation at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about something scheduled, you use the Simple Present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It will be extraordinary and it is for a good cause.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">We are going to go axe-throwing. What else are you going to be doing on Sunday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> So where are we going?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It starts at 1:00 p.m.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "And when will our team axes and axe-throwing shirts be here?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What else are you going to be doing on Sunday?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " You use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous</span> tense to talk about  an action that's happening at a specific time in the future.<br/> When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous</span>, the action will have started before that moment ( 4 p.m.)  in the future, and it  will continue beyond that moment (4 p.m.). ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I will be working at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and be working at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span> tense to talk about an action in the future which comes before another action in the future.  <br>When using the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the Future Perfect as similar to the Present Perfect tense.  However, you are looking into the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You can call me at the office after 8 a.m. <span class=\"strong\">I will have got </span> to work by 8.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The train will depart the station at 9 a.m. You will arrive at the station at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the train <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">On Sunday at 1:00 p.m., I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be laying</span> on my sofa.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll have done</span> all my chores by 10:00 a.m. on Sunday.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "On Sunday at 1:00 p.m., I will be on my sofa and I will be planning to either take a nap or eat a snack. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will have finished all my work on Saturday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The tickets will have arrived by Friday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When will our team axes and axe-throwing shirts be here?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write about some future plans you have made with friends. It can be real or imaginary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Answer questions like: What are you doing? When will you go? Who will you be going with? What kind of activities will you be doing? What is the timetable?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use your answers to write up your plans using the Future Tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your description of your plan should be 100 words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your description aloud to a partner and compare stories.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Who has the more interesting plan?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk in details about future plans with friends.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write the full information about my plans in 100 words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use future tenses to talk about plans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my written piece with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le18ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le18ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>  : Well, speaking of friends, this friend has got you guys two tickets to a charity event this weekend.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>  : Oooooo. Exciting! I'm in.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>  : V. You're so generous. So where are we going ? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>  : We are going to go ... axe-throwing.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>  : Huh? I'm out.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>  : Um. What is it?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span> : It is like throwing darts, but instead of darts you throw axes. Doesn't it sound amazing?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Nope. Still out.<br />", "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob02re2img05.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter! Listen! You get into teams; five people a team and you play and keep score. It will be extraordinary and it is for a good cause.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: When is it?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: This Sunday. It starts at 1:00 p.m.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I can go. I will have finished all my work on Saturday and I figure I'll have done all my chores by 10:00 a.m. on Sunday.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Good. The tickets will have arrived by Friday.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: And when will our team axes and axe-throwing shirts be here?<br />", "time": "33000"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You are right. He is a jerk. C'mon Peter. What else are you going to be doing on Sunday?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, let's see. On Sunday at 1:00 p.m., I will be on my sofa and I will be planning to either take a nap or eat a snack. Right now. It's a toss up.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh. Didn't I mention that the tickets are on the house?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Ooooo. I'm in again.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You are truly baffling.<br />", "time": "60500"}], "coverimg": "engenn9le18ob02re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about friendship, emotions and behavior.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about future action.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What do you and your friends usually do together?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Are you doing anything with your friends in the near future?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Next week? Next month?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "What do you and your friends like to do together?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I had lots of <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">chores</span> to do everyday. I <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_1\">figure</span> they would take me hours!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">\"Chores\"</span> are routine tasks usually i